    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n114011" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χῑλιό-ναυς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ὁ, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of a thousand ships,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					352
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ χ. Ἑλλάδος Ἄρης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					106
				</span></i>
			 (eleg.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλάταις χιλιόναυσιν,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χιλίαις ναυσί</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>IA</u>
				174
			</span></i> (lyr.); also in later Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. στόλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					13.1.27
				</span></i>
			.</div>
